The right of way was lifted in 1925-26 and is not tagged as a railway anywhere in OpenStreetMap, so this is traced along the shore-road corridor the line ran on or beside: 2.06 km on Beach Avenue out of Ontario Beach, then 7.49 km on Edgemere Drive along the bluff and the barrier beach between Lake Ontario and Long Pond, Cranberry Pond and Braddock Bay, then a 1.71 km straight leg standing in for the trestle across the mouth of Braddock Bay -- no modern road crosses there -- and 0.19 km on Manitou Beach Road to the Manitou Beach terminus. Two further chords of 0.49 km and 0.30 km bridge gaps in the Edgemere Drive geometry. Traced length 11.44 km (7.11 miles) against a documented 8 miles: the shortfall is mostly the straight bay crossing and the barrier-beach wiggle the roads do not reproduce.", "segments": [{"start": 1908, "end": 1925, "headway_min": 60, "note": "Final operator, 1908-1925. The last car ran in 1925 and the track was lifted soon after -- an early example of the interurban abandonments that followed across the country. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_View_Beach_Railway", "https://www.frrandp.com/2019/07/a-railway-on-lake-ontario-grand-view.html"]}]}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-77.60861, 43.25828], [-77.60857, 43.25834], [-77.60856, 43.25839], [-77.60858, 43.25845], [-77.60862, 43.25849], [-77.60867, 43.25852], [-77.60874, 43.25857], [-77.60912, 43.2588], [-77.60931, 43.2589], [-77.60952, 43.25903], [-77.60965, 43.25911], [-77.60979, 43.25921], [-77.60985, 43.25925], [-77.61058, 43.25973], [-77.61069, 43.2598], [-77.61142, 43.26025], [-77.61183, 43.2605], [-77.61336, 43.26152], [-77.61455, 43.26232], [-77.61504, 43.26264], [-77.61